      <h2>My C Programming Project: Pyramid Pattern</h2>
      <p>This beginner-level C program prints a pyramid using stars (*). It uses simple <strong>for loops</strong> and <strong>printf()</strong>.</p>

      <h3>C Program</h3>
      <pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;

int main() {
    int i, j, rows;

    printf("Enter number of rows: ");
    scanf("%d", &amp;rows);

    for (i = 1; i &lt;= rows; i++) {
        for (j = 1; j &lt;= rows - i; j++) {
            printf(" ");
        }

        for (j = 1; j &lt;= 2 * i - 1; j++) {
            printf("*");
        }

        printf("\n");
    }

    return 0;
}</code></pre>

      <h3>Logic of the Program</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Read the number of rows from the user.</li>
        <li>The first loop controls the rows of the pyramid.</li>
        <li>The second loop prints spaces before the stars.</li>
        <li>The third loop prints stars in each row.</li>
        <li>After printing each row, <code>printf("\n")</code> moves to the next line.</li>
        <li>The program stops after all rows are printed.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Step-by-Step Example</h3>
      <p>If the user enters <strong>5</strong>, the output is:</p>
      <pre><code>    *
   ***
  *****
 *******
*********</code></pre>

